    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0965" n="955" xml:id="pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">646G.9331/7–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-30T15:00:00+08:00">July 30, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 30—6:35 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2971.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Hinke<anchor n="8" xml:id="d894-f1"/> has observed apparent reluctance on part
                    British Minister (Commercial)<anchor n="9" xml:id="d894-f2"/> to take seriously
                    need for realistic rational export controls at Hong Kong, a problem which will
                    become pressing once Communists take Canton. Until British agree to some
                    effective supervision over Hong Kong exports to Communist China, western powers
                    will obviously lack essential economic leverage for dealing with Communists on
                    important problems. Unaware any satisfactory substitute for export controls at
                    Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d894-f1" n="8" xml:id="d894-f1-content">
                <p>Frederick W. Hinke, Consul and Commercial Attaché in China at Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d894-f2" n="9" xml:id="d894-f2-content">
                <p>John Colville Hutchison.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
